## Why this step duplicates `00_config`'s code instead of importing it

Each Ruby step directory (`ruby/00_config`, `ruby/01_struct_skeleton`, ...) is
a fully self-contained gem — its own `Gemfile`/`.lock`, its own copy of
`lib/boukensha/{config,tasks}.rb`, unchanged from step to step. There is no
shared Ruby gem that later steps depend on. To stay parity-first (see
`00_config`'s stated principle: "plan is parity, not redesign"), each Python
step directory should be the same: a fully self-contained `uv` project, not a
path-dependency on the previous step's package. This repo also has no
uv-workspace file at the root, reinforcing that steps are meant to stand
alone.

So `01_struct_skeleton`'s Python package copies `config.py`, `errors.py`, and
`tasks/` forward verbatim from `00_config` and adds `tool.py`, `message.py`,
`context.py` on top — mirroring exactly what the Ruby side does.

